<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5341" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bĭlībris</span></b> , e
		bilibra, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>of two pounds.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			Adj.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>Weighing two pounds</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">offae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					18, 11, 26, § 103</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mullus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					3, 45, 5</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Containing two pounds</i>: aqualis, * <i><span class="en">Plaut. Mil.
				3, 2, 39</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cornu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 2, 2, 61</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Subst., <i>a quantity of two pounds</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Veg. Vet. 3, 6, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 6,
				10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Apoc. 6, 6</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>